00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:28.550
<i>The Suicide Squadron and Milady Sochie fought against the powerful squad of FLATs.</i>

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:35.030
<i>Meanwhile, I was trying to persuade the one single person who refused to flee the battlefield, the old woman, Anis.</i>

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.780
<i>That was when I discovered that she was related to the baker who employed Keith.</i>

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.730
<i>It was quite a shock to me.</i>

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:52.130
<b>Dianna's Desperate Fight</b>

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.660
Is that a Pigeon?

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.870
Ahh, it's our little Blue Bishop.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.580
You're pretty smart if you can deliver a letter to us like that.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.580
Loran, we've received a message.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:33.540
Is it bad?

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.750
Just the opposite.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.920
Miashei's been sent to the war hospital, they say it's nothing to worry about.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:38.920
Thank goodness.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.430
On the other hand, it looks like Dianna Counter is on the move to attack the ship at Kingsley.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.470
I knew it.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.850
Do you think the hospital might also be in danger?

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:49.190
You mean they can't just move the hospital?

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:52.550
That would require moving a lot of sick and wounded soldiers.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.780
What if we launched an attack on the Soleil before they attacked us?

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.650
What do you mean?

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.440
The one who strikes first is often the one who wins, right?

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.830
The Soleil's trapped and can't move right now. It's the best time for an attack.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:05.910
That might be, however...

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.660
Sochie, please think that through first.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.040
I did think it through.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.960
Regardless of whether it's a hit and run attack, or all out war, our enemy's not just mindless machines.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.340
You have to think of the people living there.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.510
We can't just charge in there and kill everything indiscriminately...

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.550
Sister, you've been acting strangely!

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:22.640
Lady Sochie...

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.550
Sister, have you forgotten?

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.640
Our father was murdered by the Moonrace!

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.850
How could you spout such idealistic crud!?

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.050
My Sister is...

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.940
You've become soft and weak ever since you started hanging around Loran!

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.240
I'll never forget our father's death!

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.450
Milady! I will find a way to protect the hospital...

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.660
...and also a way to win the battle!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.360
Damn it!

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.460
What Sochie says isn't exactly wrong...

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.830
But there's not much she can do about it at this point.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.540
Queen Dianna...

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.380
Boss!

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.350
What's up, you guys?

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:16.060
We're friends of the Captain. We'd like to come on board and work here.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.860
Friends of the Captain?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.940
We're pleased to be at your service and meet you.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.900
Pleased to meet you as well. I am Horace, the lead technician.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.120
l am Jacop, and that jerk is Bruno.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.730
Pleased to meet you.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.870
Shit... We can't even use a ladder to climb down from here...

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.250
The White Mustache's wandering around outside right now.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.840
Couldn't we just take control of the ship?

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:44.050
There's nobody here...

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.430
They're way too relaxed.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.350
Now's our chance... why don't we just activate and steal the entire hovercraft?

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.760
Idiot...

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.310
What are you guys doing here?

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.520
Is that Captain Loran?

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.440
We met you at that donkey and old granny's house.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.150
What are you doing here?

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.450
Our buddy Horace said that if we didn't have any place to go...

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.490
That we could stay here and work.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.740
You're friends with Mr. Horace?

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:14.460
He said that the captain was just about to leave and that we should take the helm for him.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.320
That'd be great!

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.050
Damn you!

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.550
Piece of shit...!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.150
Couldn't you say something when you're sitting there like that?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.940
That's really rude.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.730
I'm sorry, Sochie.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.830
You have to consider the geopolitical factors in our situation.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.460
Are you saying that we should consider land structure and climates as a factor in our politics?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.630
Precisely.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.380
If you closely follow the territorial borders we've marked on our map, our intent should become obvious to anyone.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.840
Can you honestly say that now, after making that speech?

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.930
Our plan was progressing too rapidly and recklessly, so it became a necessity.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.840
Am I right?

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:29.350
Our opponents still intend to fight, despite my attempts.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.330
That's where you've been.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.660
What's going on?

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.540
It's our duty to protect you and to keep bad things from happening.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.710
We'll escort you back to your room.

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:43.450
I'd like to speak to Lieutenant Harry.

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:55.640
Are you telling me that, after I entrusted Genganam to him, Agrippa Maintainer and his followers betrayed us?

00:06:55.850 --> 00:07:00.230
The times started changing ever since our operation to return here began.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:04.190
It seems that Agrippa Maintainer and his followers also changed their way of thinking.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:08.690
Whatever the case, it seems like those who maintain the moon's hibernation capsules have changed their attitude.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:13.020
After being on the moon for so long, perhaps his own fighting instincts have reawakened.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:17.280
In that case, they must feel that a person like myself is no longer important.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.250
It is true that on the day of Dianna's Speech,

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.210
There was an attempt to assassinate you.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.420
And then there was Corin.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.430
That might also be connected to the assassins who were trying to sneak in.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.350
Would it?

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:39.410
These people who do not want to come to earth... Why would they want to expand the war?

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:43.150
They may be trying to increase the general sentiments against you here.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.360
If that's true, I'll need to consider this matter carefully.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.230
Yes.

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.320
One more thing, Harry. Let me ask a favor of you.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.230
Yes?

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:52.030
The guardsmen on duty around my room, replace them with women.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.820
It looks as though you've overlooked something.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:54.780
Ah... right.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.740
It doesn't matter how much time goes by, I am still a woman.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:01.150
It's depressing to always be surrounded by stoic male guards.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:16.970
Would it be alright for me to enter the hospital first?

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:20.850
Be aware, the manager will yell at you if you make too much noise.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.840
Just keep going, the hospital is straight ahead.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.330
Sochie!

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.130
Miashei!

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:52.460
Some people here are on the road to heaven, keep your voice down!

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:53.630
Oh, sorry.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.630
Forgive us, we're not familiar with these kinds of things.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.850
You came to see me!

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.140
Of course I would!

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.420
I don't think she should be this energetic...

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.150
It's nothing but a broken bone, there's no need for such noise.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.720
Cecily, come here and make this pumpkin calm down.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.560
Don't yell!

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.240
This place is its own battlefield.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.530
We're lucky that we do our fighting 'inside' the Kapools.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.740
I can see...

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:39.680
Ahh, I see. So you've already visited the hospital camp Miashei's being kept in?

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.930
That's right. And we also wanted to see how things were coming along here.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.430
That's the reason we all came here.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:48.060
As you can see, we've set up some security measures around here,

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.150
but our defenses simply are not very strong.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.150
When Guin Rhineford comes...

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:54.860
l intend to ask him about setting up a stronger guard.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.450
Will he be coming here?

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.530
In that case, let me speak to him as well.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.150
It's here!

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:10.130
I had no idea Lily Borjarno would also be meeting us here.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:13.960
Now that all of the ladies are here, we should have a party, shouldn't we?

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.420
But unfortunately, since our spaceship is still buried...

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.540
We can't throw a party in the sky just yet.

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:23.930
Sir Guin, show me around the inside.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.640
Guin Rhineford...

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.940
I'd like to discuss us redeploying so we can guard the hospital.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:31.650
Let's hold any talk of war until after Lady Lily has left us, Laura.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:32.650
Right.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.440
You should all join us.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.030
She's way out of line.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.240
Out of line?

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.990
As the Duke's daughter, her behavior's not the least bit appropriate.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:44.980
Amazing! There are so many pretty lights!

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.950
Laura, what do you think?

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:50.750
l believe this artifact might be from an era before the White Doll's time.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.460
That's exactly what I thought.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.040
This is amazing.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.920
I wonder how school teachers are going to teach their students history now?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.550
That's a good thought.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.840
Do you believe that it will really fly?

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:05.930
Our technicians from the Moonrace have promised us so. This will become our most valuable weapon.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:09.850
Valuable weapon? Aren't you thinking a bit rashly?

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.060
You think so?

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:13.150
Perhaps I should just call it reckless.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:16.730
It's said that the first steps to all changes in history are like that.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.440
Sir Guin, I'd like you to oversee our emplacements.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.660
Chief Ladderum, come with me. You as well, Laura.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.020
Right!

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:29.750
Come to think of it, I've never asked you your name.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.120
Oh, I'm Kihel Heim.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:36.190
So your the Miner's daughter?

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:40.250
Right, but I've never seen them excavate a ship like this!

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:41.800
- You're fairly cocky, aren't you.
- Hmm?

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:46.010
Naturally. What status do you have that gives you the right to act so familiar with Sir Guin?

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.350
My status?

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:52.940
That's right. You should try showing more discretion and just focus on doing more work.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.430
Doing work?

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:10.200
Is there anything you need me to do for you?

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:14.290
Well, let's see, what exactly are you good at?

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.790
Are you a great typist, or mathematician?

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.000
Nothing like that...

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.210
That's no good, then...

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:22.590
I have an idea! Why don't you go and volunteer for the hospital?

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.090
The hospital?

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:26.350
I don't know anything about medicine.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.510
That has nothing to do with it.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:30.180
They need more people there.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:34.020
Their doctors and nurses are overwhelmed by the influx in wounded soldiers.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:36.100
They don't even have time for food.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.400
Thank you so much, Lady Lily Borjarno!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.310
You've shown me something that's very important!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:48.480
I've been such a fool, I wasn't able to figure out something even as simple as this!

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:54.000
Please, Chief Nurse.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:56.080
Do you have any experience in nursing?

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.670
l don't even know how to cook a fish...

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.010
"That just won't do"...is what I wish I could say.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.260
Throw this garbage into the hole in the valley.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.210
Yes.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.600
Cecily, dress this girl properly...

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.720
...and show her how to handle the laundry.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:11.880
Sure!

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:15.690
Wash this as well, and return it to its place.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.160
Yes.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.690
Thanks for the help. Now, your dress...

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:23.750
And your job is to avoid giving us even more injured people!

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:24.900
Right!

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.610
Pull that off, and we might finally be able to go home.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.610
I will do my best!

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.500
Your hair will only get in the way of your job.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.080
Now we'll head over and change the sheets.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:36.540
Right.

00:13:41.650 --> 00:13:43.340
Alright!

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:48.090
Don't give me more work to do!

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.710
I'm sorry!

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:01.010
I can't even do this very well...

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.190
Hey Mr. Horace, the electricity...

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.610
The electrical voltage has been fixed.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:11.320
Did you find the open circuit between numbers 23 and 25?

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:14.790
We set the voltage to a fixed rate, so it should be stable now.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.790
That makes sense.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:19.290
Those two people are hard workers.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.090
Yeah. Now in order to be sure if we can start up the I-Field...

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:26.720
...we'll need to know what capacity the electrical circuits can handle to be sure it'll even work at all.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.590
l switched it just as it said in the manual.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:34.680
The nano-skin has kept this thing perfectly intact, possibly for well over a thousand years.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:40.010
It's possible that the machine itself might even have that self repair function. It could even move on its own someday.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.400
It's full of glass vials, so it's heavy.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.810
Right.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.330
The medicine is extremely valuable. Don't drop it.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.980
Alright, next.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:57.620
Who exactly are you?

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:01.210
I am the daughter of this hospital's sponsor.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:04.000
You mean you're the daughter of Luzianna's Duke?

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.090
That's right.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.880
I've come to ask about the girl who came to work for you today.

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:10.720
Has Kihel Heim done something wrong?

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.090
No.

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:15.310
She feels that she's not being pushed hard enough.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:18.720
The minor tasks you've given her won't help her to advance her potential nursing career.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.890
Although, perhaps I'm asking too much of you.

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.790
- That's enough!
- I don't want this!

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:41.790
- Are you ready?
- Yes!

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:45.290
Please, don't! No, stop this!

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.170
Get him more whiskey.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:49.000
Don't give me more sake! Just get me the anesthetic!

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:51.300
Prepare an anesthetic injection.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.640
Right.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:55.620
- Tie down his arms and legs and then clear the room.
- Right.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.730
- It's the one on the right.
- Okay.

00:15:57.730 --> 00:16:02.390
- I'll do anything! Just let me go!
- Cecily, hurry it up.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.020
Sorry, I couldn't find the bucket for the blood.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.320
- Tie his hands up.
- Right!

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.820
Get his legs ready.

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.320
I love this leg, please let me go!

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.020
Alright! Don't worry, once we give you the anesthetic, you won't feel a thing.

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:16.490
The injection! Now!

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.620
What are you doing, girl?

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.500
Nurse, cut away his pants.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.000
I'll even treat my mother better. Please don't do this!

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:30.300
- I'll leave it to you, Doctor. Do it delicately.
 -You can count on me.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.210
Mother!

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:36.210
- Place that bucket under his bed.
- Right.

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:42.180
Alright, we'll begin the operation to amputate his leg.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:53.810
She's only carrying dirty laundry?

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.430
I guess I was wrong. This seems to have gone as planned...

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:10.620
Kihel- Kihel Heim!

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:13.800
Another team's soiled linens are ready for you...

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.220
We'll need them to be prepared by tonight.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:18.090
Got it, ma'am.

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:21.310
Wow, that cart's totally full!

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.840
I wonder if she'll make it by tomorrow...

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:26.390
That miner's daughter is pretty strong.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:29.900
I think we'd be better off just burning them all.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.610
Don't be a fool.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.990
Who knows when more supplies will come in again.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.780
Do I have to finish them all today?

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:36.860
Use the cart to move them.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:39.400
And it's fine if you get them done by tomorrow.

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:43.190
Done by tomorrow.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:48.710
The doctor told me...

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:55.010
...that the reason why there's dirty things soiled with blood and sweat...is because these people are still alive.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:59.090
l never thought of it that way before.

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:33.200
Hmm? What is it?

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.510
Queen Dianna...

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.290
Nice legs, lady!

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:42.100
What in the world are they making you do!?

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:44.310
Just look and you'll understand.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.020
- Let me help you!
- This is something I must do.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:50.060
And it would destroy Miss Kihel's reputation if I were to quit now.

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:54.820
B-but...Is that batch all that you have to get done?

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.320
You have to finish all of that, right?

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:57.610
That's exactly right.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.520
I'll get it done by tomorrow if I work the whole day, right?

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:02.780
Loran Cehack?

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:03.870
Right...

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:06.410
Because this is for the sake of those who are still alive...

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.960
There'll be even more dirty clothes tomorrow.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.710
That's right...

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.700
l need to finish it by morning.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.410
Damn fool!

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:24.710
Loran?

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:29.270
Hey, Loran, what are doing, Loran?

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:33.900
Gallop, I'm just going to take the White Doll for something,

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:35.480
...but it's not a battle.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.690
Loran sent us a transmission.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:38.490
He's taking off?

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:40.690
I'm just heading off to do some laundry.

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:47.910
Loran, if there's no enemy, don't bother using the White Doll!

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:50.290
Machines are supposed to be used to help people.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.780
Fighting isn't the only thing they're used for.

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:59.120
Milady, use this as a washing machine.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:01.800
A washing machine? What are you talking about?

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.580
Hop on shore.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:12.690
Are you going to use White Doll's hands?

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:16.390
That's exactly it. I can even put the bucket in.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:23.610
I wish we had some soap powder in there.

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:25.620
It might overflow, so please get back.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.110
Right!

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:37.700
It can spin backwards, and move the water in all directions.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:48.710
Soap bubbles?

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:52.440
Did you put in some soap?

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.100
No, I didn't know about it. The soap had to be in the cart.

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:59.020
The person who gave me the load must have thrown some in with it.

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:01.530
That might be it.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:03.990
But how about this... perhaps after seeing all of your efforts, Milady...

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.490
...God decided to reward you for them!

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:10.490
You really think that could ever happened to me, Loran Cehack?

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:14.700
Of course it could!

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:22.710
What's with you and the "Lady"...

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:28.800
I've been informed that Commander Phil just deployed,

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:31.810
With a large attack squadron, and he intends to destroy their spacecraft.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:34.020
That appears to be true.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:37.810
There is a girl named Kihel Heim who may be on that ship.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.610
Yes.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.980
I'd like her to be brought here.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:44.610
Are you officially requesting me to do it?

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:46.600
I believe you're the best man for the job.

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:49.910
Understood.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.190
I wish you success.

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.390
Such beautiful colors...

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.170 --> 00:23:44.270
<i>Dianna Counter intends to destroy the Spacecraft being excavated by the Militia.</i>

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:47.110
<i>Lieutenant Harry is told of this...</i>

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:50.800
<i>...and posing as a technician, comes to take back Queen Dianna.</i>

00:23:51.350 --> 00:23:54.700
<i>However, it does not turn out as he had desired...</i>

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:57.240
<i>...and Milady Kihel's idea fails.</i>

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:01.120
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:02.920
Harry's Trouble

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.450
"The wind will go wherever it wishes."

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Harry's Trouble</b>
